IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`
IMPORT fixtures

§ `Terms and Conditions governing the HSBC Revolution Credit Card Reward Points Programme`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENT. hsbc-revolution-reward-points-tnc: "Terms and Conditions governing
-- the HSBC Revolution Credit Card Reward Points Programme", "Effective from 1
-- April 2026" (HSBC Bank (Singapore) Limited), cl.1-17. The Programme period
-- "starts from 1 April 2026 until terminated by HSBC" (cl.2). The guidance FAQ
-- (hsbc-revolution-faq) is undated.
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT SAYS.
--   cl.4       Qualifying Transactions are POSTED retail purchases, less a list of
--              exclusions (cl.4 bullets) and a list of excluded MCCs (cl.4.2).
--   cl.5       "Selected Contactless Payments" = Qualifying Transactions "made via
--              Visa contactless through a contactless terminal mode which
--              includes Visa payWave, Apple Pay, Google Pay and Samsung Pay".
--   cl.6       "Selected Online Transactions" = Qualifying Transactions "made via
--              the internet and processed by the respective merchants/merchant's
--              acquiring bank as an online transaction type through the Visa
--              Worldwide networks, including credential-on-file payments ... HSBC
--              determines whether a transaction is a Selected Online Transaction
--              based on system indicators which are determined by the merchants
--              and the merchant's acquiring bank."
--   cl.7       "Eligible Transactions" = Selected Contactless Payments and
--              Selected Online Transactions "that fall within any one of the
--              following MCCs": 49 rows in three groups (travel, department
--              stores and retail, dining excluding hotel dining, transport and
--              membership clubs).
--   cl.7.1     1 Base Point per SGD1 of the Eligible Transaction, plus 9 Bonus
--              Points, or 19 Bonus Points "if the Cardholder maintains a Deposits
--              ADB of at least SGD50,000 in the Eligible EGA Account for the
--              calendar month in which the Eligible Transaction was posted".
--   cl.7.2     "Reward points shall be calculated based on the total amount of
--              Eligible Transactions posted ... within each qualifying calendar
--              month, rounded down to the nearest SGD1." Bonus Points are capped
--              at 9,000 per calendar month, or 22,800 with the ADB. Base Points
--              are uncapped.
--   cl.8       1 Reward point per SGD1 on all other Qualifying Transactions.
--   cl.9       The most a SGD1 of Eligible Transaction can earn is 20 points.
--   cl.10      Base Points credited by statement cycle; Bonus Points by the last
--              day of the following calendar month.
--
-- NO CONVERSION TO MILES IS HELD. The terms speak of Reward points and refer to
-- "HSBC's Rewards Programme terms and conditions", which are not held. The
-- answer's miles are NOTHING; any rate in miles per S$1 is a conversion that
-- no held document states.
--
-- THE FORKS.
--   F-hsbc-faq: the FAQ says "With effect from 15 July 2024, contactless payment
--     transactions will earn 1 HSBC Reward point". The terms effective 1 April
--     2026 restore contactless (cl.5, cl.7). The module takes the terms, which
--     are dated and later; the FAQ is undated.
--   F-hsbc-tax: cl.4 excludes "Tax payments (except HSBC Tax Payment Facility)";
--     the Facility has no fact in the ontology, so a tax payment through it is
--     not modelled (MCC 9311 is excluded as listed).
--   F-bill-payments does not arise: HSBC's list names AXS and utilities, not bill
--     payments as such; a bill paid on the card at a non-excluded MCC earns the
--     1-point Qualifying rate.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `cl.4 -- what is not a Qualifying Transaction`

-- cl.4.2, in the table's order (48 rows; row 29 is 7995).
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Revolution excluded category codes` MEANS
    LIST 4829, 4900, 5199, 5960, 6010, 6011, 6012, 6050, 6051, 6211, 6300, 6513,
         6529, 6530, 6532, 6533, 6534, 6536, 6537, 6538, 6540, 6555, 7299, 7399,
         7349, 7511, 7523, 7801, 7995, 8062, 8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299,
         8398, 8651, 8661, 8999, 9211, 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405, 9754

-- cl.4 bullets, by kind of charge. HSBC's list has no "bill payment" bullet:
-- AXS and utilities are the named bills. Instalment: "The monthly instalment
-- amounts under all card instalment plan" and "Total purchase amount under HSBC
-- 0% Instalment Payment Plan and HSBC PayLater Instalment Plan".
GIVEN k IS A `Charge kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Revolution cl.4 excludes the kind` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `Retail purchase`                                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Bill payment`                                      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Bill paid directly to the biller on the card`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Top-up of a prepaid card or stored-value account`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Payment of funds to a payment service provider`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Instalment plan charge`                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `My Preferred Payment Plan charge`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Cash advance`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Balance transfer or funds transfer`                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Fee, interest or finance charge`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Pre-authorisation`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Payment through UOB Payment Facility`              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `NETS or NETS-related transaction`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `SmartPay or personal loan`                         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Transit-related transaction`                       THEN FALSE

-- cl.4 bullets that name counterparties: money payments/transfers (Paypal, SKR
-- skrill.com, CardUp, SmoovPay, iPayMy), top-ups of prepaid cards, stored-value
-- cards or e-wallets (EZ-Link, Transitlink, NETS Flashpay, Youtrip), AXS.
GIVEN d IS A Descriptor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Revolution cl.4 names the description` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `AXS`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `PayPal`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Skrill`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `CardUp`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SmoovPay`                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `iPayMy`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `EZ-Link`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Transit Link`             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `FlashPay`                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Youtrip`                  THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                            FALSE

-- cl.4: Qualifying Transactions are POSTED retail purchases; "unposted,
-- cancelled, disputed and refunded transactions" are out.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Revolution purchase is not a Qualifying Transaction` p MEANS
    `Revolution cl.4 excludes the kind` (p's `charge kind`)
    OR `the code is among` p `the Revolution excluded category codes`
    OR `Revolution cl.4 names the description` (p's descriptor)
    OR p's `posting status` EQUALS `Authorised but not posted`
    OR p's `later reversed`


§§ `cl.5, cl.6, cl.7 -- Eligible Transactions`

-- cl.5: contactless terminal mode: the physical card or a wallet token tapped
-- on a reader. Magnetic Secure Transmission is not a contactless terminal mode.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is a Selected Contactless Payment` p MEANS
    p's presentation EQUALS `Physical card tapped on a reader`
    OR p's presentation EQUALS `Wallet tapped on a reader`

-- cl.6: a purchase made via the internet; HSBC decides by the merchant's indicator.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase was made via the internet` p MEANS
    p's presentation EQUALS `Card number entered online`
    OR p's presentation EQUALS `Wallet used in an app or on a website`
    OR p's presentation EQUALS `Card details held on file by the merchant`
    OR p's presentation EQUALS `Recurring payment arrangement`

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchase is a Selected Online Transaction` p MEANS
    `the purchase was made via the internet` p AND p's `merchant indicator` EQUALS `Flags online`

-- cl.7: the 49 MCC rows. Travel: 3000-3350 airlines, 3351-3500 car rental,
-- 3501-3999 lodging; and 4511 airlines, 4411 cruise lines, 7011 lodging.
-- Department stores and retail: 4816, 5045, 5262, 5309, 5310, 5311, 5331, 5399,
-- 5611, 5621, 5631, 5641, 5651, 5655, 5661, 5691, 5699, 5732-5735, 5912, 5942,
-- 5944-5949, 5964-5969, 5970, 5992, 5999. Dining excluding hotel dining: 5441,
-- 5462, 5811, 5812, 5813. Others: 4121 taxicabs, 7997 membership clubs.
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Revolution Eligible category codes` MEANS
    LIST 4511, 4411, 7011, 4816, 5045, 5262, 5309, 5310, 5311, 5331, 5399,
         5611, 5621, 5631, 5641, 5651, 5655, 5661, 5691, 5699, 5732, 5733, 5734,
         5735, 5912, 5942, 5944, 5945, 5946, 5947, 5948, 5949, 5964, 5965, 5966,
         5967, 5968, 5969, 5970, 5992, 5999, 5441, 5462, 5811, 5812, 5813, 4121,
         7997

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the code of the purchase is an Eligible code` p MEANS
    `the code is among` p `the Revolution Eligible category codes`
    OR `the code is from` p 3000 3350
    OR `the code is from` p 3351 3500
    OR `the code is from` p 3501 3999


§§ `cl.7.1, cl.7.2 -- the rates, the caps and the monthly rounding`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Revolution Base Points per SGD1 of an Eligible Transaction` MEANS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Revolution Bonus Points per SGD1 without the ADB` MEANS 9

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Revolution Bonus Points per SGD1 with the ADB` MEANS 19

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Revolution Bonus Points cap per calendar month without the ADB` MEANS 9000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Revolution Bonus Points cap per calendar month with the ADB` MEANS 22800

GIVEN h IS A `Revolution holder`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Revolution Bonus Points per SGD1 for` h MEANS
    IF h's `Deposits ADB of S$50,000 in the sole Everyday Global Account`
    THEN `Revolution Bonus Points per SGD1 with the ADB`
    ELSE `Revolution Bonus Points per SGD1 without the ADB`

GIVEN h IS A `Revolution holder`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Revolution Bonus Points cap for` h MEANS
    IF h's `Deposits ADB of S$50,000 in the sole Everyday Global Account`
    THEN `Revolution Bonus Points cap per calendar month with the ADB`
    ELSE `Revolution Bonus Points cap per calendar month without the ADB`

-- cl.7.2: the points follow the month's TOTAL of Eligible Transactions rounded
-- down once. A purchase's share is the rise in the rounded total.
GIVEN before IS A NUMBER
      amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole SGD1 this purchase adds to the month's Eligible total` before amount MEANS
    (FLOOR (before PLUS amount)) MINUS (FLOOR before)


§§ `The answer when the code and indicator are settled`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Revolution points per SGD1 on other Qualifying Transactions` MEANS 1

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Revolution holder`
      m IS A `Revolution month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Revolution answer on an Eligible Transaction` c p h m MEANS
    `an answer for` c `in` `HSBC Reward points` `of` (`Revolution points on an Eligible Transaction` p h m) `to` (`Revolution points on an Eligible Transaction` p h m) `wanting` ((`the Revolution Bonus Points per SGD1 for` h) TIMES (`the whole SGD1 this purchase adds to the month's Eligible total` (m's `Eligible Transactions posted`) (p's `amount in SGD`))) `at` NOTHING `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `Revolution bonus` `depending on` (`Revolution ADB conditions for` h) `per` "HSBC Revolution T&C cl.7.1-7.2"

GIVEN h IS A `Revolution holder`
GIVETH A LIST OF Condition
`Revolution ADB conditions for` h MEANS
    IF h's `Deposits ADB of S$50,000 in the sole Everyday Global Account`
    THEN LIST `HSBC: the Deposits ADB holds for the whole calendar month`
    ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Revolution holder`
      m IS A `Revolution month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Revolution points on an Eligible Transaction` p h m MEANS
    (`the whole SGD1 this purchase adds to the month's Eligible total` (m's `Eligible Transactions posted`) (p's `amount in SGD`))
    PLUS (min ((`the Revolution Bonus Points per SGD1 for` h) TIMES (`the whole SGD1 this purchase adds to the month's Eligible total` (m's `Eligible Transactions posted`) (p's `amount in SGD`)))
              (`at least nothing` ((`the Revolution Bonus Points cap for` h) MINUS (m's `Bonus Points earned`))))

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Revolution answer on another Qualifying Transaction` c p MEANS
    `an answer for` c `in` `HSBC Reward points` `of` (FLOOR (p's `amount in SGD`)) `to` (FLOOR (p's `amount in SGD`)) `wanting` 0 `at` NOTHING `excluded` FALSE `drawing on` `No pot` `depending on` EMPTY `per` "HSBC Revolution T&C cl.8"

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Revolution holder`
      m IS A `Revolution month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Revolution answer when the code and indicator are settled` c p h m MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Revolution purchase is not a Qualifying Transaction` p
            THEN `nothing is earned on` c `in` `HSBC Reward points` `per` "HSBC Revolution T&C cl.4"
        IF (`the purchase is a Selected Contactless Payment` p OR `the purchase is a Selected Online Transaction` p) AND `the code of the purchase is an Eligible code` p
            THEN `Revolution answer on an Eligible Transaction` c p h m
        OTHERWISE `Revolution answer on another Qualifying Transaction` c p

-- The two stand-ins for an indicator she cannot see.
GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Revolution holder`
      m IS A `Revolution month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Revolution answer when the indicator flags card-present` c p h m MEANS
    `Revolution answer when the code and indicator are settled` c (`reflagged purchase` p `Flags card-present`) h m

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Revolution holder`
      m IS A `Revolution month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Revolution answer when the indicator flags online` c p h m MEANS
    `Revolution answer when the code and indicator are settled` c (`reflagged purchase` p `Flags online`) h m

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Revolution holder`
      m IS A `Revolution month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`Revolution answer when the code is settled` c p h m MEANS
    IF `the purchase was made via the internet` p AND p's `merchant indicator` EQUALS `Indicator not known`
    THEN `bracketed from` (`Revolution answer when the indicator flags card-present` c p h m) `to` (`Revolution answer when the indicator flags online` c p h m) `adding` (LIST `The merchant's indicator is not known`)
    ELSE `Revolution answer when the code and indicator are settled` c p h m

`a Revolution code that is excluded` MEANS 4829
`a Revolution code that is Eligible` MEANS 5812

GIVEN c IS A Card
      p IS A Purchase
      h IS A `Revolution holder`
      m IS A `Revolution month`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`HSBC Revolution earns on` c p h m MEANS
    IF `the code is unknown for` p
    THEN `bracketed from` (`Revolution answer when the code is settled` c (`recoded purchase` p `a Revolution code that is excluded`) h m) `to` (`Revolution answer when the code is settled` c (`recoded purchase` p `a Revolution code that is Eligible`) h m) `adding` (LIST `The merchant category code is not known`)
    ELSE `Revolution answer when the code is settled` c p h m


§§ `The clock the Revolution bonus pot runs on`

-- cl.7.1-7.2 ("posted ... within each qualifying calendar month").
GIVETH A `Period basis`
`the Revolution bonus pot's period` MEANS `Calendar month`

GIVETH A `Date basis`
`the Revolution bonus pot's date basis` MEANS `Posting date`

#ASSERT `the Revolution bonus pot's period` EQUALS `Calendar month`
#ASSERT `the Revolution bonus pot's date basis` EQUALS `Posting date`


§§ `Illustrations -- built from cl.7.1, cl.7.2 and cl.9`

`the Revolution card` MEANS `HSBC Revolution`
`a holder without the ADB` MEANS `Revolution holder` WITH `Deposits ADB of S$50,000 in the sole Everyday Global Account` IS FALSE
`a holder with the ADB` MEANS `Revolution holder` WITH `Deposits ADB of S$50,000 in the sole Everyday Global Account` IS TRUE

GIVEN posted IS A NUMBER
      bonus IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Revolution month`
`a Revolution month with` posted `of Eligible Transactions and` bonus `Bonus Points` MEANS
    `Revolution month` WITH
        `Eligible Transactions posted` IS posted
        `Bonus Points earned`          IS bonus

`a fresh Revolution month` MEANS `a Revolution month with` 0 `of Eligible Transactions and` 0 `Bonus Points`

`S$100 tapped at a restaurant` MEANS `the base purchase`
`S$100 by Apple Pay tapped at a restaurant` MEANS `purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Wallet tapped on a reader`
`S$100 online at a department store` MEANS `purchase paid by` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5311) `Card number entered online`
`S$100 online at a department store, indicator flagged online` MEANS `reflagged purchase` `S$100 online at a department store` `Flags online`
`S$100 online at a department store, indicator not known` MEANS `reflagged purchase` `S$100 online at a department store` `Indicator not known`
`S$100 online at a department store, indicator flagged card-present` MEANS `reflagged purchase` `S$100 online at a department store` `Flags card-present`

-- cl.7.1: 1 Base + 9 Bonus = 10 points per SGD1: S$100 earns 1,000.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 by Apple Pay tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
-- ... with the ADB: 1 + 19 = 20 per SGD1: 2,000 (cl.9: "the maximum ... is 20 Reward points").
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder with the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT elem `HSBC: the Deposits ADB holds for the whole calendar month` ((`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder with the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `depends on`)
#ASSERT null ((`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `depends on`)
-- ... no held conversion to miles.
#ASSERT isNothing ((`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `miles certain`)

-- cl.7.2: the cap. 9,000 Bonus Points a month. With 8,950 earned, S$100 earns 100 Base + the 50 of room = 150.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` (`a Revolution month with` 1000 `of Eligible Transactions and` 8950 `Bonus Points`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 150
-- ... with the cap full, the Base alone: 100.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` (`a Revolution month with` 1000 `of Eligible Transactions and` 9000 `Bonus Points`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
-- ... with the ADB the cap is 22,800.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder with the ADB` (`a Revolution month with` 1200 `of Eligible Transactions and` 22700 `Bonus Points`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder with the ADB` (`a Revolution month with` 1200 `of Eligible Transactions and` 22800 `Bonus Points`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
-- The bonus wanted before the cap: 9 x 100 = 900 without the ADB.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` (`a Revolution month with` 1000 `of Eligible Transactions and` 9000 `Bonus Points`))'s `bonus units before cap` EQUALS 900
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s pot EQUALS `Revolution bonus`

-- cl.7.2: rounded down once on the month's total. A S$4.80 tap on a fresh month adds 4 whole dollars -> 4 Base + 36 Bonus = 40;
-- the next S$4.80 takes the total from 4.80 to 9.60: floor 9 less floor 4 = 5 -> 50.
`S$4.80 tapped at a restaurant` MEANS `purchase for` `the base purchase` 4.80
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$4.80 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$4.80 tapped at a restaurant` `a holder without the ADB` (`a Revolution month with` 4.80 `of Eligible Transactions and` 36 `Bonus Points`))'s `units certain` EQUALS 50
-- ... under S$1 a single purchase can earn nothing: S$0.80 on a fresh month.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`purchase for` `the base purchase` 0.80) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 0

-- cl.7: only the listed MCCs. Fast food (5814), a supermarket (5411), pet shops (5995), beauty (5977), OTAs (4722)
-- and SimplyGo (4111) are not listed: they earn the 1-point Qualifying rate (cl.8): S$100 -> 100.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5814) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5411) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5995) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5977) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4722) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4111) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
-- ... and the listed ones earn the bonus: airlines 3000..3350 and 4511, lodging 3501..3999 and 7011, car rental 3351..3500, taxis 4121, clubs 7997, bakeries 5462, bars 5813, caterers 5811.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 3001) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4511) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 3400) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 3700) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 7011) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4121) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 7997) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5462) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5813) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5811) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5262) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 5964) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
-- cl.7: 3350/3351 and 3500/3501 and 3999/4000 are the range edges.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 3350) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 3351) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 3999) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4000) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100

-- cl.5/cl.7: paying by chip (inserted) at a listed MCC is not contactless: the Qualifying rate.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Physical card inserted or swiped`) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100

-- cl.6: online at a department store (5311), indicator flagged online: Eligible.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 online at a department store, indicator flagged online` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000
-- ... flagged card-present by the acquirer: the Qualifying rate, though the cardholder typed it online.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 online at a department store, indicator flagged card-present` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
-- ... indicator unknown: floor 100, ceiling 1,000, the condition named.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 online at a department store, indicator not known` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 online at a department store, indicator not known` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units at best` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT elem `The merchant's indicator is not known` ((`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` `S$100 online at a department store, indicator not known` `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `depends on`)
-- ... credential-on-file counts as online when the indicator says so.
#ASSERT (`HSBC Revolution earns on` `the Revolution card` (`purchase paid by` `S$100 online at a department store, indicator flagged online` `Card details held on file by the merchant`) `a holder without the ADB` `a fresh Revolution month`)'s `units certain` EQUALS 1000

